      "name": "FIFO2",
      "module_name": "release_fifo2",
      "parent_id": null,
      "behavior": "Two-entry FIFO of unsigned8-bit bytes. FIFO holds at most two bytes, without empty bypass or full simultaneous-pop lookahead. Push eligibility uses old occupancy<2; pop uses old occupancy>0. Apply old head removal before accepted append; reset flushes. FIFO output is zero when empty, valid iff nonempty, ready iff not full. Sample active-low rst_pipe_n synchronously only at rising edges of clk_pipe. No asynchronous reset response. Expose a valid/ready input stream and a valid/ready output stream, preserving stalled head data.",
      "test_expectations": "Use the independent saved16-cycle contract for reset flush, full/empty boundaries, ordering, stalls and simultaneous transfers. Preserve every specified output, including invalid-cycle data.",
      "constraints": {
        "latency_cycles": 1,
        "protocol": "valid_ready"
      },
