    "behavior": "FIFO holds at most two bytes, without empty bypass or full simultaneous-pop lookahead. Push eligibility uses old occupancy<2; pop uses old occupancy>0. Apply old head removal before accepted append; reset flushes. FIFO output is zero when empty, valid iff nonempty, ready iff not full. XOR is combinational: data_o=data_i XOR 165 at all times, valid_o=valid_i, ready_o=ready_i; clock/reset do not add state or gate the combinational function. System output is FIFO head XOR165, including165 when empty; no extra XOR latency. Instantiate exactly one adopted release_fifo2 and one adopted release_xor_byte. Connect the saved valid/ready streams directly along the explicit graph, with reverse ready. Share clk_pipe and synchronous active-low rst_pipe_n; do not add top state, bypass, data transformation or latency."
  },
